WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:03.680
You three are mages?

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:06.110
From the field program, then.

00:00:06.110 --> 00:00:07.290
What?

00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:08.570
You know about that?

00:00:08.890 --> 00:00:14.910
Of course the residents of the target village 
for the program would know about it.

00:00:15.310 --> 00:00:16.700
Are you simpletons?

00:00:18.510 --> 00:00:19.610
I beg your pardon.

00:00:19.610 --> 00:00:24.040
I held ill will for witches 
for a long time. It was reflexive.

00:00:24.370 --> 00:00:26.410
Wh-What a jerk.

00:00:26.410 --> 00:00:27.170
Shh!

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:30.840
These people protected me.

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:31.920
Oh, my...

00:00:32.370 --> 00:00:35.370
You confronted the mercenary 
and did not run?

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:37.310
Somewhat reckless of you.

00:00:37.310 --> 00:00:43.060
U-Um, what's going on here? 
Who is that beastfallen?

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:44.940
Leave this place.

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:46.030
What?!

00:00:46.570 --> 00:00:49.020
That beastfallen is a guard,

00:00:49.490 --> 00:00:52.420
who solidifies the witch's 
control over this village.

00:02:23.450 --> 00:02:27.960
It was two years ago that control 
of the village changed hands.

00:02:25.240 --> 00:02:27.960
Episode 4            I'm Not Afraid to Die

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:31.100
The witch who was to be your supervisor

00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:35.700
surrendered the village to an invader 
without a fight and vanished.

00:02:36.410 --> 00:02:39.590
Ever since, no one has been 
able to oppose her.

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:42.240
Wh-What's the deal?

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:44.250
Does the Headmaster know?

00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:47.810
Wh-What's the point
 of sending us here if—

00:02:49.860 --> 00:02:52.480
Of the five special program students,

00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:55.640
three were working 
with the anti-witch faction,

00:02:56.450 --> 00:02:59.130
one is a badly-behaved beastfallen,

00:03:00.020 --> 00:03:02.780
and one is a remedial student.

00:03:03.230 --> 00:03:06.150
We're all problems for the Academy.

00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:10.200
Y-You mean... she took students 
she wanted to be rid of

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:11.920
and sent them to the field program?

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:17.070
Would going back to the Academy now 
mean we flunk and get expelled?

00:03:17.070 --> 00:03:18.550
It wouldn't, right?

00:03:18.550 --> 00:03:20.970
Why do something so roundabout when—

00:03:20.970 --> 00:03:22.710
Not fulfilling one's duties

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:26.600
is a serious issue in large organizations.

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:28.580
Damn it!

00:03:28.580 --> 00:03:31.730
Then why don't we go notify the Church 
& Mage Army and defeat the witch?

00:03:31.730 --> 00:03:37.470
Battling a powerful witch 
could mean losing 1,000 soldiers.

00:03:37.470 --> 00:03:39.070
It's not worth it to them.

00:03:39.070 --> 00:03:42.480
The Church & Mage Army doesn't 
operate based on profit and loss!

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:46.830
In these parts, they call 
themselves the Church Knights.

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:50.210
The troubles of a witch village

00:03:50.210 --> 00:03:52.330
would not move them in the slightest.

00:03:53.490 --> 00:03:55.460
Why would you trust him?

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:58.250
Do you not find him fishy?

00:03:58.820 --> 00:04:03.930
What proof do you have that this priest 
is not in league with that beastfallen?

00:04:03.930 --> 00:04:05.530
Professor Los.

00:04:05.530 --> 00:04:07.830
But the father here is blind...

00:04:07.830 --> 00:04:09.710
What does that matter?

00:04:09.710 --> 00:04:12.740
I look like no more than 
an <i>adorable</i> young girl,

00:04:12.740 --> 00:04:14.310
but in fact I am a renowned

00:04:15.190 --> 00:04:16.810
witch.

00:04:16.810 --> 00:04:19.660
In the absence of sufficient 
reason for trust,

00:04:19.660 --> 00:04:22.070
I maintain skepticism.

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:26.280
A sudden appearance 
followed swiftly by rudeness.

00:04:26.740 --> 00:04:32.410
That beastfallen knew 
 I was the students' escort.

00:04:32.780 --> 00:04:34.650
'Tis strange, is it not?

00:04:34.650 --> 00:04:39.380
What aspect of mine adorable visage 
would have suggested that?

00:04:39.380 --> 00:04:44.930
But what if the Arbiter who attacked us 
ran back to the Church and provided intel?

00:04:45.270 --> 00:04:50.370
And then a priest shared that information 
from the Church with the witch?

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:53.480
I see. Suspicious indeed.

00:04:53.480 --> 00:04:55.940
If you encounter someone so suspicious,

00:04:56.240 --> 00:04:59.360
wouldn't the effective strategy 
be to kill them immediately?

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:01.620
'Twould be simple to kill them.

00:05:01.620 --> 00:05:05.570
However, I am fond of careful 
scrutiny of the circumstances.

00:05:05.570 --> 00:05:08.650
If thou insist thou art not our enemy,

00:05:08.650 --> 00:05:10.830
show us around the village.

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:13.490
I should like to see 
the villagers' reactions.

00:05:14.140 --> 00:05:15.410
As you please.

00:05:19.420 --> 00:05:21.820
Daddy!

00:05:23.130 --> 00:05:24.780
Laios!

00:05:25.640 --> 00:05:28.390
You're safe. I was so worried!

00:05:28.390 --> 00:05:32.180
It's all right. He is unharmed, Uls.

00:05:32.180 --> 00:05:33.750
Father.

00:05:33.750 --> 00:05:35.230
Who are these kids?

00:05:35.230 --> 00:05:40.350
Field program students, apparently. 
They protected Laios from the mercenary.

00:05:40.950 --> 00:05:43.780
This is the field program village...

00:05:43.780 --> 00:05:46.390
Thank you for bringing my boy back.

00:05:47.100 --> 00:05:49.590
Father, is the danger to the village past?

00:05:49.590 --> 00:05:50.390
Yes.

00:05:51.130 --> 00:05:56.620
However, these folks appear to 
suspect me of working for the witch.

00:05:56.620 --> 00:06:00.180
Yeah, you do seem fishy.

00:06:00.180 --> 00:06:03.840
Still, that's quite some 
bad luck you guys have.

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:05.380
But don't lose heart!

00:06:05.830 --> 00:06:08.240
Oh, you must be tired from your journey.

00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:11.470
Even if you're going back, 
you should rest for the night.

00:06:12.050 --> 00:06:14.720
And that's the school over there!

00:06:14.720 --> 00:06:17.670
Wow, you have a school.

00:06:17.670 --> 00:06:21.350
We take care of the orphaned 
kids as a village.

00:06:21.350 --> 00:06:24.270
I'm the only kid who was 
born in the village.

00:06:24.690 --> 00:06:28.450
When I was born, 
the nice witch lady did a spell

00:06:28.450 --> 00:06:30.410
so everyone would like me!

00:06:30.410 --> 00:06:32.490
She told me so.

00:06:32.490 --> 00:06:36.070
That's why I'm the most 
precious child in the village!

00:06:36.970 --> 00:06:38.760
Oh, um,

00:06:38.760 --> 00:06:41.330
I'm talking about the previous witch lady.

00:06:42.080 --> 00:06:45.750
Remember the barrier in the forest? 
She made that, too!

00:06:46.150 --> 00:06:48.130
'Twas a marvelous barrier.

00:06:48.460 --> 00:06:51.680
Yes. She was the pride of the village.

00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:53.390
If that witch was so great,

00:06:53.390 --> 00:06:56.190
how come she fled without fighting?

00:06:56.190 --> 00:06:57.060
Hey!

00:06:57.520 --> 00:07:02.900
I just don't know. She'd been with us 
since the founding of the village.

00:07:04.940 --> 00:07:07.750
'Tis very quiet around here.

00:07:07.750 --> 00:07:10.990
We hardly ever get any 
strangers visiting, so...

00:07:11.890 --> 00:07:14.910
Here we are. This is it.

00:07:17.490 --> 00:07:19.660
Wh-What are those?

00:07:20.610 --> 00:07:21.890
Dolls.

00:07:21.890 --> 00:07:25.040
One for each person who used to live here.

00:07:25.040 --> 00:07:27.690
<i>Used</i> to live here?

00:07:28.010 --> 00:07:29.880
Well...

00:07:30.790 --> 00:07:33.610
The witch and the mercenary 
aren't bad people,

00:07:33.610 --> 00:07:36.010
but they don't tolerate escape.

00:07:36.340 --> 00:07:39.620
The sight of those dolls stops 
people from trying to run.

00:07:39.620 --> 00:07:42.610
Except for the kids who don't 
remember two years ago.

00:07:43.310 --> 00:07:45.980
But life ain't that bad here.

00:07:45.980 --> 00:07:48.940
If ya follow the rules, 
it's calm and peaceful.

00:07:51.670 --> 00:07:53.740
See ya later!

00:07:54.200 --> 00:07:56.800
I see...

00:07:56.800 --> 00:07:58.200
Yes.

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:04.960
I <i>see</i>...

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:07.070
Very well!

00:08:09.230 --> 00:08:10.670
Let us kill the witch.

00:08:13.290 --> 00:08:15.800
And Albus, while we're at it.

00:08:15.800 --> 00:08:16.810
What now?!

00:08:16.810 --> 00:08:18.550
P-Professor?!

00:08:18.550 --> 00:08:22.020
Killing the Headmaster won't solve anything!

00:08:22.020 --> 00:08:24.390
But 'tis infuriating!

00:08:24.390 --> 00:08:25.750
That damned Albus!

00:08:25.750 --> 00:08:27.320
She duped not only you three,

00:08:27.320 --> 00:08:29.860
but <i>me</i> as well!

00:08:30.300 --> 00:08:36.410
Oh, right. If there's no supervising witch, 
your job can't end.

00:08:36.410 --> 00:08:38.240
Precisely.

00:08:38.240 --> 00:08:39.100
So...

00:08:42.060 --> 00:08:44.610
The more I think about it, 
the more it infuriates me!

00:08:44.610 --> 00:08:47.880
The lass made a total fool of me!

00:08:48.180 --> 00:08:50.550
Listen up, my ducklings!

00:08:50.550 --> 00:08:53.420
I swear to complete my job!

00:08:53.690 --> 00:08:55.930
I'll teach her

00:08:55.930 --> 00:08:59.720
what happens if thou 
underestimate the Dawn Witch!

00:09:05.010 --> 00:09:07.930
My goodness. Youngsters these days.

00:09:07.930 --> 00:09:10.480
Utterly lacking in passion and drive.

00:09:10.860 --> 00:09:14.990
I'm pissed, too. 
But there's nothing I can do.

00:09:14.990 --> 00:09:20.240
If we go back to Wenias, maybe the 
Church & Mage Army will help us!

00:09:20.240 --> 00:09:21.140
But...

00:09:22.490 --> 00:09:26.180
If we do that, the village 
is sure to become a battlefield.

00:09:27.510 --> 00:09:32.460
I'm not sure it's right to do that 
to the village just so we can graduate.

00:09:33.560 --> 00:09:35.470
Th-That's...

00:09:35.990 --> 00:09:39.450
Which is why I feel we 
should do this on our own.

00:09:39.450 --> 00:09:40.470
What?

00:09:41.180 --> 00:09:45.230
The fact that she let us into 
the village means she isn't wary of us.

00:09:45.630 --> 00:09:49.730
With me around, 
you two can cast without limit.

00:09:49.730 --> 00:09:51.440
And we even have Professor Los!

00:09:51.860 --> 00:09:55.740
And if I grab the Staff of Ludens again, 
it can at least serve as a distraction—

00:09:55.740 --> 00:09:57.440
That's enough!

00:10:00.810 --> 00:10:04.040
The beastfallen in the forest 
has clearly seen war.

00:10:04.040 --> 00:10:06.500
Imagine the sort of witch he works for.

00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:11.500
You're telling us to die in a fight 
we have no shot at winning!

00:10:11.500 --> 00:10:15.170
C-Calm down! That's not what Sayb meant.

00:10:15.170 --> 00:10:18.760
Who cares! It's what he said!

00:10:19.170 --> 00:10:22.130
So we just sit back and get expelled?

00:10:22.130 --> 00:10:24.890
If that happens, we'll have 
our memories erased.

00:10:25.400 --> 00:10:28.520
Including all memory of this journey, 
and of everyone else.

00:10:29.060 --> 00:10:31.720
Then I'll be empty.

00:10:33.320 --> 00:10:35.980
You'd die to avoid starting over?

00:10:37.780 --> 00:10:39.490
I realized something

00:10:39.490 --> 00:10:44.440
when we were attacked by the Arbiter 
and I decided to use the Staff of Ludens.

00:10:50.170 --> 00:10:53.210
I'm not afraid to die.

00:10:57.620 --> 00:10:59.490
But just the thought scares me.

00:11:00.800 --> 00:11:02.840
I'm sorry. Of course it does.

00:11:03.140 --> 00:11:07.350
You and Kudo can leave 
the village and wait, then.

00:11:08.870 --> 00:11:10.600
What are you talking about?

00:11:13.130 --> 00:11:15.040
I was telling you

00:11:15.040 --> 00:11:17.860
that I don't want you to die!

00:11:18.500 --> 00:11:21.200
Huh? Why?

00:11:25.280 --> 00:11:27.470
Huh? Um...

00:11:29.540 --> 00:11:30.290
Hort!

00:11:30.290 --> 00:11:32.740
What is the point of chasing after her?

00:11:33.130 --> 00:11:35.150
To apologize, of course.

00:11:35.150 --> 00:11:40.710
"I don't know what I did, 
but I'll just apologize." Is that it?

00:11:40.710 --> 00:11:43.220
'Tis an awful kind of apology.

00:11:43.540 --> 00:11:47.690
Excessively low regard for thyself 
can at times hurt others.

00:11:48.590 --> 00:11:53.350
Kudo, educate this numbskull 
about why Hort cried.

00:11:55.620 --> 00:11:57.940
It's because you're friends.

00:11:58.230 --> 00:11:59.510
What?

00:11:59.510 --> 00:12:03.370
Hort just doesn't want her 
friend to die like a dog.

00:12:03.820 --> 00:12:08.930
But you couldn't see why she would be sad.

00:12:08.930 --> 00:12:10.250
Friends...

00:12:13.400 --> 00:12:15.960
I don't want Hort to die, either.

00:12:16.440 --> 00:12:18.450
I'm going to apologize!

00:12:20.120 --> 00:12:21.830
Ah, youth.

00:12:25.900 --> 00:12:28.220
What kind of mage am I?

00:12:28.600 --> 00:12:31.530
This just screams "one of 
the Church's faithful."

00:12:32.140 --> 00:12:33.500
Is that bad?

00:12:38.570 --> 00:12:41.950
D-Do you live here?

00:12:42.370 --> 00:12:45.450
I'm Lilly. I was cleaning.

00:12:45.450 --> 00:12:49.830
O-Oh, I see. I'm sorry for interrupting.

00:12:50.270 --> 00:12:53.710
Th-There's no rain. 
Why are you dressed like that?

00:12:53.710 --> 00:12:57.430
Um, I'm supposed to stay out of sight.

00:12:57.430 --> 00:12:59.880
But... you were crying.

00:12:59.880 --> 00:13:02.630
Oh, um, I...

00:13:03.090 --> 00:13:04.490
Are you sad?

00:13:04.490 --> 00:13:09.060
No, no. I just had a fight with a friend.

00:13:09.060 --> 00:13:10.390
Oh.

00:13:11.330 --> 00:13:15.860
Um, it's okay for a mage 
to follow the Church.

00:13:16.930 --> 00:13:19.940
The father says that all the time.

00:13:21.740 --> 00:13:25.210
Hey, Lilly, do you love the father?

00:13:25.210 --> 00:13:26.000
Huh?

00:13:26.000 --> 00:13:28.220
H-How did you know?

00:13:28.220 --> 00:13:29.370
Lilly.

00:13:32.430 --> 00:13:33.930
Father...

00:13:35.200 --> 00:13:38.250
Hey, do we have a shot?

00:13:38.620 --> 00:13:39.870
I couldn't say.

00:13:39.870 --> 00:13:42.670
Then what's the point of fighting?

00:13:42.910 --> 00:13:44.670
To live.

00:13:45.030 --> 00:13:47.510
My purpose in life is entertainment.

00:13:47.510 --> 00:13:50.040
And right now, mine entertainment

00:13:50.040 --> 00:13:51.210
is you three!

00:13:52.580 --> 00:13:57.560
These past few days, I have completely 
inhabited the role of teacher.

00:13:57.890 --> 00:14:01.190
The ducklings I have protected and guided

00:14:01.190 --> 00:14:04.190
are about to be cruelly 
brought crashing down to earth.

00:14:04.730 --> 00:14:07.320
I detest simplistic tragedies.

00:14:07.990 --> 00:14:13.490
I shan't allow anyone to trample upon 
my beloved students' denouement.

00:14:14.430 --> 00:14:17.310
If it is to obtain the ending I desire,

00:14:18.660 --> 00:14:22.170
then I shall be willing to die.

00:14:26.080 --> 00:14:29.670
My goodness. I told her not to come out.

00:14:30.680 --> 00:14:33.890
She comforted me because I was crying.

00:14:34.300 --> 00:14:36.860
So please, don't scold her.

00:14:37.640 --> 00:14:40.560
Are you in a position to worry about others?

00:14:40.560 --> 00:14:41.570
Huh?

00:14:42.530 --> 00:14:44.830
I heard you had a fight with a friend.

00:14:44.830 --> 00:14:46.900
Y-You heard that?

00:14:47.410 --> 00:14:49.760
I have excellent hearing.

00:14:50.440 --> 00:14:52.410
It's not a big deal.

00:14:53.040 --> 00:14:55.090
I just...

00:14:57.500 --> 00:14:59.790
Of course. I...

00:14:59.790 --> 00:15:02.660
I should have used my words.

00:15:03.190 --> 00:15:07.260
Sayb just didn't understand. 
I didn't have to get so upset.

00:15:08.390 --> 00:15:10.740
I'm sure they're all worried about me.

00:15:10.740 --> 00:15:12.720
I'll just use my words.

00:15:12.720 --> 00:15:14.670
I better head back now.

00:15:16.110 --> 00:15:16.950
Huh?

00:15:16.950 --> 00:15:19.280
How utterly careless of you.

00:15:19.280 --> 00:15:23.480
Going off alone in a village 
controlled by a witch.

00:15:25.170 --> 00:15:26.570
<i>His cane...</i>

00:15:27.890 --> 00:15:29.280
<i>That symbol...</i>

00:15:29.850 --> 00:15:31.450
<i>Dia Ignis!</i>

00:15:31.840 --> 00:15:33.810
Speaking of fights,

00:15:33.810 --> 00:15:36.450
I heard you betrayed the Church.

00:15:37.050 --> 00:15:39.690
I don't blame you.

00:15:40.270 --> 00:15:44.290
You attended a mage academy 
for four whole years.

00:15:44.670 --> 00:15:47.380
Of course it had an effect on you.

00:15:47.740 --> 00:15:53.360
Furthermore, the Tyrant's barbaric 
nature is difficult to condone.

00:15:54.430 --> 00:15:56.850
<i>I-I can't move!</i>

00:15:57.810 --> 00:16:00.680
Let's have a little conversation.

00:16:06.940 --> 00:16:09.070
S-Somebody!

00:16:09.070 --> 00:16:11.440
Shh. Quiet.

00:16:12.460 --> 00:16:16.040
If your heart is righteous,

00:16:16.710 --> 00:16:19.660
then no one will be hurt.

00:16:20.890 --> 00:16:23.360
Thou art unable to find Hort?

00:16:23.360 --> 00:16:25.420
Correct. I've looked everywhere.

00:16:25.880 --> 00:16:28.380
Did any of the villagers see anything?

00:16:31.420 --> 00:16:35.050
There's no other option. 
We'll track her magic.

00:16:35.550 --> 00:16:37.900
Are you sure this is the right way?

00:16:37.900 --> 00:16:41.380
I can track any mage I have met.

00:16:41.730 --> 00:16:44.390
But why would she be in this forest?

00:16:45.950 --> 00:16:49.080
It appears she must be in there.

00:16:49.080 --> 00:16:50.820
A cave?!

00:16:52.320 --> 00:16:53.860
Wow!

00:16:53.860 --> 00:16:56.800
The cave is lit up! How convenient!

00:16:56.800 --> 00:16:57.950
Amazing!

00:16:58.400 --> 00:17:01.080
So you can cast Solm 
with no incantation, too.

00:17:01.080 --> 00:17:02.740
Of course I can!

00:17:02.740 --> 00:17:07.460
One day, I'll be able to cast any spell 
without doing the incantation.

00:17:10.260 --> 00:17:11.400
Professor Los?

00:17:13.700 --> 00:17:14.750
Blood.

00:17:15.750 --> 00:17:22.770
And the magical traces I sense 
from further in don't belong to Hort alone.

00:17:22.770 --> 00:17:26.020
Shit, this is a trap! Let's retreat!

00:17:26.020 --> 00:17:27.740
No, this is perfect.

00:17:27.740 --> 00:17:28.770
What?!

00:17:27.740 --> 00:17:28.770
Huh?

00:17:29.560 --> 00:17:33.390
If the village's ruler 
is granting us an audience,

00:17:33.390 --> 00:17:36.610
then let's graciously 
accept the offer, shall we?

00:17:36.610 --> 00:17:39.680
Are you stupid?! We'll be killed!

00:17:39.680 --> 00:17:41.620
A battle with a witch

00:17:41.620 --> 00:17:45.290
is all about evading 
the traps she has laid out.

00:17:45.630 --> 00:17:49.490
My dear Ludens and 
I shall discern those traps.

00:17:49.490 --> 00:17:53.250
That still won't change the fact 
 we're at a disadvantage!

00:17:53.640 --> 00:17:57.300
The Church & Magic Army does 
not fear fighting witches.

00:17:57.950 --> 00:18:00.300
The symbol of that army is

00:18:00.300 --> 00:18:03.010
the king of a lost nation destroyed by a dragon,

00:18:03.010 --> 00:18:04.750
the Dragon Conqueror King.

00:18:04.750 --> 00:18:07.500
He found victory 
in a seemingly hopeless fight

00:18:07.500 --> 00:18:09.980
and became the master of a dragon.

00:18:10.290 --> 00:18:14.570
Wilt thou be a daring and resolute
 soldier or a fleeing civilian?

00:18:15.100 --> 00:18:18.280
The choice is thine.

00:18:21.030 --> 00:18:22.650
This is stupid!

00:18:22.650 --> 00:18:24.290
I ain't goin' along with this!

00:18:24.630 --> 00:18:26.910
I'm not as strong 
as the Dragon Conqueror King

00:18:26.910 --> 00:18:30.290
and charging to an obvious 
death isn't bravery!

00:18:30.290 --> 00:18:32.640
I don't care if I'll be expelled!

00:18:32.640 --> 00:18:34.000
Kudo!

00:18:34.390 --> 00:18:37.340
It seems I didn't push hard enough.

00:18:37.340 --> 00:18:39.760
Sayb, light, please.

00:18:45.330 --> 00:18:46.470
Damn it!

00:18:46.770 --> 00:18:48.670
You abandoned them?

00:18:51.010 --> 00:18:53.080
Y-You...

00:18:53.080 --> 00:18:56.060
If you cut ties with them,

00:18:56.060 --> 00:18:58.880
then how about joining <i>me</i>?

00:18:59.760 --> 00:19:02.570
You'll be able to learn magic.

00:19:02.860 --> 00:19:04.110
What?

00:19:04.740 --> 00:19:07.940
Chapter of Harvest, verse one, Solm!

00:19:07.940 --> 00:19:09.240
Grant me power!

00:19:09.240 --> 00:19:10.810
My name is Saybil!

00:19:16.970 --> 00:19:19.100
What the devil was that? An explosion?!

00:19:19.100 --> 00:19:20.470
S-Sorry, Professor.

00:19:22.760 --> 00:19:25.860
Thou hast not the least bit of control.

00:19:25.860 --> 00:19:27.470
Sorry.

00:19:27.740 --> 00:19:30.400
If <i>I</i> could use magic...

00:19:31.780 --> 00:19:35.230
I believe I've had a great idea.

00:19:36.170 --> 00:19:40.110
Real witches can create magic.

00:19:40.110 --> 00:19:42.790
That includes my employer.

00:19:42.790 --> 00:19:46.240
I-I only want to join 
the Church & Mage Army.

00:19:46.990 --> 00:19:50.120
There's no point learning 
magic if I'm expelled.

00:19:50.120 --> 00:19:52.960
I can get you into the Army.

00:19:52.960 --> 00:19:53.980
What?!

00:19:53.980 --> 00:19:55.970
Is that true, old man?

00:19:55.970 --> 00:19:57.380
"Old man?"

00:19:57.890 --> 00:20:03.700
If you accept the conditions, I'll enter 
into a witch's blood contract with you.

00:20:07.260 --> 00:20:08.470
Whaddya say?

00:20:09.020 --> 00:20:10.310
Where's Hort?

00:20:10.310 --> 00:20:11.310
Huh?

00:20:11.730 --> 00:20:13.440
What did you do with Hort?

00:20:13.870 --> 00:20:15.450
Hort?

00:20:15.450 --> 00:20:17.690
Oh, the girl with the hat.

00:20:19.160 --> 00:20:20.940
I killed and ate her.

00:20:22.680 --> 00:20:24.950
She tasted great.

00:20:24.950 --> 00:20:29.310
The flesh of young women is so tender.

00:20:32.390 --> 00:20:34.580
You cur!

00:20:34.580 --> 00:20:36.460
Over my dead body!

00:20:36.460 --> 00:20:39.470
Fine. Get lost, then.

00:20:39.470 --> 00:20:43.670
It's a pain, but I gotta kill your friends.

00:20:44.090 --> 00:20:45.390
Hold it!

00:20:48.320 --> 00:20:51.810
You're not going anywhere! You hear me?

00:20:53.370 --> 00:20:56.560
I like your spunk. You pass.

00:20:56.560 --> 00:20:58.440
Or so I'd like to say,

00:20:59.360 --> 00:21:03.190
but first let's see what you've got!

00:21:03.970 --> 00:21:06.030
There's nothing here.

00:21:06.030 --> 00:21:07.320
No traps.

00:21:07.320 --> 00:21:08.830
It seems not.

00:21:08.830 --> 00:21:10.590
'Tis conciliation.

00:21:11.080 --> 00:21:14.480
An apprentice mage with limitless magic.

00:21:14.480 --> 00:21:17.570
Any witch would want thee,

00:21:17.570 --> 00:21:20.340
including the witch 
of this village, I dare say.

00:21:21.880 --> 00:21:23.840
The witch wants me?

00:21:31.240 --> 00:21:32.560
Sayb!

00:21:33.150 --> 00:21:35.830
I-I'm fine.

00:21:36.530 --> 00:21:39.230
I think I just remembered something.

00:21:40.890 --> 00:21:42.630
Listen, Sayb.

00:21:43.430 --> 00:21:46.490
None would blame thee 
if thou turnst back.

00:21:46.490 --> 00:21:47.490
What?

00:21:48.070 --> 00:21:50.350
There is no shame in running.

00:21:50.350 --> 00:21:54.120
Thou value thine own life too lightly.

00:21:54.520 --> 00:22:00.310
Wouldst thou try to save Hort alone, 
even if I were against it?

00:22:01.810 --> 00:22:03.210
I would.

00:22:03.690 --> 00:22:04.960
Why?

00:22:06.900 --> 00:22:13.100
Hort is a... f-friend. That's why.

00:22:14.480 --> 00:22:16.590
Ah, friendship.

00:22:17.470 --> 00:22:20.500
I, too, had that once.

00:22:20.500 --> 00:22:22.830
Y-You are, too, Professor.

00:22:27.350 --> 00:22:31.780
I would try to save you, as well. 
Without question.

00:22:35.380 --> 00:22:37.060
My goodness!

00:22:37.060 --> 00:22:39.690
Thou art certainly a sweet-talker!

00:22:39.690 --> 00:22:41.130
Professor Los.

00:22:41.130 --> 00:22:43.780
There are people who care for thee.

00:22:43.780 --> 00:22:46.460
There are people thou carest for.

00:22:46.460 --> 00:22:48.450
Never forget that.

00:23:00.530 --> 00:23:01.590
Sayb!

00:23:04.040 --> 00:23:05.400
Ludens!

00:23:14.180 --> 00:23:16.010
Ow!

00:23:16.010 --> 00:23:17.660
That was right in the stomach!

00:23:17.660 --> 00:23:20.570
I warned you, didn't I?

00:23:21.140 --> 00:23:22.700
That if you have suspicions,

00:23:24.200 --> 00:23:26.020
you should kill me.

00:23:55.830 --> 00:23:56.990
What's going on?

00:23:56.990 --> 00:23:58.920
Did I die? Tell me! Tell me!

00:23:57.830 --> 00:24:09.880
<b>Next Episode       "I Decide Who's Worthy"</b>

00:23:58.920 --> 00:24:01.580
Hort, calm down.

00:24:01.580 --> 00:24:04.080
Next time: "I Decide Who's Worthy."

00:24:04.080 --> 00:24:06.710
Address my death already!

00:24:06.710 --> 00:24:08.500
Be quiet!
